#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:7
msgid "How to write a reference"
msgstr "Cómo escribir una referencia"

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:10
msgid ""
"A reference shares your experience. It is not a verdict on another person."
msgstr ""
"Una referencia comparte tu experiencia. No es un veredicto sobre otra "
"persona."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:12
msgid "Describe what happened."
msgstr "Describe lo que pasó."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:12
msgid ""
"What did you see, hear and do together? Stay concrete, the way a camera "
"would have recorded it."
msgstr ""
"¿Qué viste, qué oíste, qué hicisteis juntos? Sé concreto/a, como lo habría "
"grabado una cámara."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:13
msgid "Speak from yourself."
msgstr "Habla desde ti."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:13
msgid "Write “I felt …” or “I was glad that …” rather than “they are …”."
msgstr "Escribe «me sentí…» o «me alegré de que…» en lugar de «es…»."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:14
msgid "Name your feelings and needs."
msgstr "Nombra tus sentimientos y necesidades."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:14
msgid ""
"“I felt uneasy because I need clear agreements” tells others more than "
"“unreliable”."
msgstr ""
"«Me sentí inquieto/a porque necesito acuerdos claros» dice más que «poco "
"fiable»."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:15
msgid "Leave out labels and judgements."
msgstr "Deja fuera etiquetas y juicios."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:15
msgid ""
"Words like rude, lazy, toxic or perfect describe your judgement, not the "
"person. Let your experience speak."
msgstr ""
"Palabras como maleducado, vago, tóxico o perfecto describen tu juicio, no a "
"la persona. Deja que hable tu experiencia."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:16
msgid "Take responsibility for your feelings."
msgstr "Hazte responsable de tus sentimientos."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:16
msgid ""
"What others do can touch your feelings; the feelings come from your own "
"needs. Say what you would have wished for."
msgstr ""
"Lo que hacen otras personas puede despertar tus sentimientos; su raíz son "
"tus propias necesidades. Di qué te habría gustado."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:17
msgid "Write as if they were reading along."
msgstr "Escribe como si la persona lo estuviera leyendo."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:17
msgid "They will. Be honest and kind at the same time."
msgstr "Lo hará. Sé sincero/a y amable a la vez."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:21
msgid "You are writing about a community"
msgstr "Escribes sobre una comunidad"

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:22
msgid ""
"You are writing about a place and a whole group of people. Describe what the "
"place and living or staying together were like for you."
msgstr ""
"Escribes sobre un lugar y todo un grupo de personas. Describe cómo viviste "
"el lugar y la convivencia o tu estancia."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:23
msgid ""
"Was your experience mainly with one person? Say so explicitly, and don't let "
"it colour your impression of the whole community: a difficult encounter with "
"one person is no reason for a negative community reference."
msgstr ""
"¿Tu experiencia fue sobre todo con una persona? Dilo explícitamente y no "
"dejes que tiña tu impresión de toda la comunidad: un encuentro difícil con "
"una persona no es motivo para una referencia negativa sobre la comunidad."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:24
msgid ""
"Even better: if that person is on ecobasa, write them a personal reference."
msgstr ""
"Mejor aún: si esa persona está en ecobasa, escríbele una referencia personal."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:28
msgid ""
"If something went wrong: have you talked about it with them? A reference is "
"not the place to settle a conflict, but it can help others to know about it. "
"If you felt unsafe, say so clearly."
msgstr ""
"Si algo salió mal: ¿lo habéis hablado? Una referencia no es el lugar para "
"resolver un conflicto, pero puede ayudar a otras personas a saberlo. Si no "
"te sentiste seguro/a, dilo con claridad."

#: gift_economy/references/templates/references/_guidelines.html:30
msgid ""
"You can edit your reference at any time, for example after you have talked "
"it through."
msgstr ""
"Puedes editar tu referencia en cualquier momento, por ejemplo después de "
"haberlo hablado."

